  {
   "line_no": 29,
   "line_kind": "bullet",
   "section": "(opening)",
   "text": "3. **bowels / inward part / liver → one `inward-parts (viscera)` level** (me'eh, qereb, splanchna, kabed). These are the OT/NT somatic seat of churning compassion and distress (\"my bowels are troubled\"; \"my liver is poured out\", Lam 2:11; *splanchna* = compassion). Grouping them avoids 4 thinly-populated levels while keeping the distinct *idea* (visceral affect) separate from heart/soul.",
   "refs": [
    {
     "as_written": "Lam 2:11",
     "kind": "verse",
     "verse": "Lam.2.11"
    }
   ],
   "answer": {
    "captured": [
